      "id": "sol.hmmt-feb-algebra-2003-p4.hmmt",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "\\(1 / 2\\)\n\nThe given expression equals \\(\\sqrt{6+4 \\sqrt{2}}-(1.5+\\sqrt{2})=\\sqrt{6+2 \\sqrt{8}}-(1.5+\\sqrt{2})\\). But on inspection, we see that \\((\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{4})^{2}=6+2 \\sqrt{8}\\), so the answer is \\((\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{4})-(1.5+\\sqrt{2})=\\) \\(2-3 / 2=1 / 2\\).",
